<title>USA: Union Texas says sets stock ownership rules.</title>
<headline>Union Texas says sets stock ownership rules.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Texas Petroleum Holdings Inc said Monday it has set a minimum stock ownership guideline for its officers and directors.</p>
<p>The company said officers and directors will be expected to own within a five-year period a certain minimum amount of the company's stock with a market value that is equal to at least one to three times their annual base salary or annual board fees.  &quot;These guidelines are evidence of our total commitment to further align the interests of our officers and directors with those of all of our shareholders,&quot; said chairman and chief executive John Whitmore.</p>
</text>
